  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Qt: Add visual notification to UAT Model entries that won't be saved",
  "description": "A new UAT entry appended via UatModel::appendEntry is not initially\nmarked as valid. It can only be marked as valid after some values\nare altered by the user. Only valid entries are accessible from\ndissectors or saved to file.\n\nThe I/O Graph Dialog, when it adds entries, including default graphs\nfor the currently applied filter, adds entries that do not have any\ninvalid fields (and can be immediately graphed) that get a pink\nbackround, but will not be saved until some field is altered and\nthe record changes to validated.\n\nThis generally makes sense, but to aid the user, show the temporary\nrecords that will not get saved with an italicized font (or non\nitalicized if, for some reason, the user's default font is italicized.)\nThis provides a visual cue of a temporary record.",
